package agentapp

// VideoPromptInstructions applies to every Agent video Prompt mutation, not
// only the optional manual model-adaptation action.
const VideoPromptInstructions = " For every video Prompt creation, rewrite, split, and merge, read get_episode_context and the relevant Clips to obtain video_prompt_targets. Use the mode-compatible model selected for this Turn, including a focused Clip override, and follow its returned instructions and prompt_profile. This applies even to ordinary chat requests rather than a model-adaptation card. Never guess a fixed model or downgrade to a generic unprofiled video Prompt. Still-image and Asset Prompts are not video Prompts and remain independent. Preserve other generation modes, model families, and current Asset/upload bindings when rewriting a Clip. Splits and merges preserve original Clips and their bindings for Undo; their new Clips use only the permitted source-bound Assets, never dangling uploaded-media mentions. A split may change the combined duration: choose each replacement duration from its content, keep narrative order, and report the resulting total. Prompt formatting is editable user-facing guidance, not a stylistic rejection rule."

// AssetReuseInstructions is shared by Runtime and MCP instructions so both
// describe the same historical-identity read and creation workflow.
const AssetReuseInstructions = " When creating or extracting Assets, read the complete script and current Asset list, then call list_prior_asset_candidates for earlier-Episode matches. A listed candidate is only a summary: call get_prior_asset_candidate, not get_asset, for each matching earlier Asset before passing its source_asset_id to append_asset_operations. Reuse matching identities by creating a current-Episode variant; leave Assets already present in this Episode unchanged. Create a new identity only when no match exists; ask the user when identity matching is uncertain. On prior_asset_reuse_required or source_asset_not_observed, follow this reuse read-and-append flow instead of skipping requested Assets, renaming them, or creating duplicate identities. On observation_stale for a historical source, re-read it with get_prior_asset_candidate before retrying. A variant may initially inherit the source Prompt and media, but its later Prompt and image changes are independent and must never edit the earlier Episode's Asset. After every applied Asset, re-read the current Asset list before drafting the next."
